Original commit body from cfb477485845eb4b1f989f4d5edc81a0cddf5c9c:

Three http_method value-space defects, each of which silently LOST a link
or an entire route. A premise-check against live code before coding
confirmed three of the filed defects, found one materially worse than
filed, and found two that no longer reproduce.

1. Route::match routes vanished entirely (worse than filed).

Laravel declares its verbs as args[0] -- Route::match(['get','post'],
'/path', ...) -- but the PHP analyzer read the route path from args[0]
unconditionally, found an array rather than a string, and skipped the
call. So this was never the filed "lossy MATCH aggregate persists in
http_method": the whole route was absent from the map, and an existing
test pinned that as expected behaviour ("currently skipped because first
arg isn't a string"). Every positional argument now shifts by one for
match (path args[1], controller args[2]) and the real verb list is
emitted comma-joined as GET,POST. A dynamically-built verb list still
falls back to the MATCH token rather than inventing verbs.

2. ALL was an unrecognized wildcard.

node-http.yaml emits literal:ALL for http.createServer catch-alls, but
the OpenAPI linker's inline check knew only ANY and *, so an ALL route
never linked where an equivalent ANY route would.

3. Comma-joined multi-method routes could never link.

framework_patterns joins a list-valued YAML method key with "," and only
the route-materializer splits it back, so the linker compared "GET,POST"
against a single verb -- never equal. This is what made fix 1's output
useful rather than merely present.

All three now route through routes.method_matches() /
WILDCARD_HTTP_METHODS in the canonical route accessor, which understands
the absent, wildcard (ANY/ALL/*) and comma-joined forms. The OpenAPI
linker delegates rather than re-implementing a partial version -- the
chokepoint shape, and the same module that already consolidated route_of
/ is_route.

The * spelling has zero producers. Kept deliberately, not removed: it is
the conventional HTTP wildcard, costs one frozenset member, and dropping
it would narrow matching for any hand-authored meta or future producer.
Now documented in the vocabulary rather than sitting as an unexplained
literal inside one consumer.

TWO FILED DEFECTS DO NOT REPRODUCE (recorded, not silently dropped):
Laravel RESOURCE / API_RESOURCE already expands to 7/5 real-verb route
symbols -- the aggregate token only labels the call-site UsageContext,
which honestly names the call that was made -- and Phoenix `resources`
already expands to its 7 routes. Both verified by live probe.

